WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.150
Beth: The way Autism is portrayed and
reported in the media is incredibly

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:09.399
powerful in educating and influencing the
public both positively and negatively.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:13.960
This can be via TV or tabloid
news, films and TV series

00:00:14.139 --> 00:00:15.860
and also across social media.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:20.180
There are also obvious and clear
difference between how individuals

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:23.450
on the spectrum were portrayed
in the past compared to today.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:28.240
Joe: While the majority of filmmakers,
TV producers, journalists and so forth,

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:30.590
do not create pieces about people with
autism to purposefully misrepresent

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:34.389
or disparage them, it still happens.

00:00:35.199 --> 00:00:39.519
There are many misconceptions associated
with Autism spectrum disorder and these

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.550
can be fueled by misrepresentation.

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:45.400
These may appear at first hand,
to be positive portrayals, however

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:48.950
this can create a belief that all
individuals with Autism are the same.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:53.530
Beth: More modern films and television
shows, portray those with autism as very

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:58.920
high functioning geniuses with quirky
personalities, or ‘mute’ or ‘savant’, but

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:03.230
they omit certain groups and don’t portray
the range of characteristics that are on

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:05.690
the spectrum perpetuating the stereotype.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:10.729
Some people therefore see individuals
with Autism as high functioning with

00:01:10.799 --> 00:01:15.550
atypical abilities, such as enhanced
ability for doing things, such as working

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:19.130
with numbers, memory, music, drawing etc.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.519
However, others just see the
behavioural issues and lack of empathy

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:27.210
that are only some of the extreme
elements involved in the spectrum.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:31.570
Joe: So we can see that Individuals
with Autism spectrum disorder face many

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:35.550
different challenges of stigmatisation
and stereotyping due to the public

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:39.310
perception more often than not created
by their portrayal in the media.

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:43.140
If the media continues to portray
Autism in a more positive way

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.419
especially reflecting the nuanced
characteristics of individuals on

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:50.700
the spectrum, society should become
more informed and tolerant and try to

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:52.600
understand the nature of the individual.

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:56.270
That would then in turn mean they
are more likely to understand

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:57.630
and appreciate the differences.

00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:02.710
Beth: Many high profile creative and
pioneering individuals of the past showed

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:07.160
signs of being on the autism spectrum to
some degree but this cannot be verified.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:11.280
However, a current prominent figure
and environmental activist in the

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:16.160
world today, who can be verified, is
Swedish teen activist, Greta Thunberg,

00:02:16.559 --> 00:02:20.790
and she is now quite open about her
autism spectrum disorder diagnosis.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:25.990
Joe: Greta started protesting at the age
of 15, about climate crisis, and developed

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:28.680
an unprecedented global movement in 2018.

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:34.460
She is known worldwide as the public
face of the ‘school climate strike

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:38.559
movement’ and has spoken about her
Asperger’s syndrome diagnosis, after

00:02:38.559 --> 00:02:40.369
she was criticised over the condition.

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:44.380
Beth: She said on Twitter, that before
she started her climate action campaign;

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:48.440
“I had no energy, no friends
and I didn’t speak to anyone.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:51.609
I just sat alone at home,
with an eating disorder.”

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:55.819
Joe: She also wasn’t open about her
diagnosis in the beginning, as she

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.569
knew people would see it as a negative.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:01.994
However, Greta doesn’t view herself as
having a disability, but instead she

00:03:01.994 --> 00:03:04.109
has a different way of seeing something.

00:03:04.109 --> 00:03:07.433
Beth: While acknowledging that her
diagnosis has limited her in the past,

00:03:07.433 --> 00:03:14.900
Greta has tweeted “I have Asperger’s
and that means I’m sometimes a bit

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:18.649
different from the norm,” and she sees
being different as having a “superpower”.

00:03:18.649 --> 00:03:20.730
Joe: For many Greta Thunberg’s diagnosis
of Asperger’s Syndrome, has not

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:24.400
lowered their opinion of her, and the
qualities and characteristics that she

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:26.710
exudes, simply make her who she is.

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:32.509
Today she continues to inspire people
around the world, young and old, with

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:36.699
or without autism, to step outside their
comfort zone and make a difference.

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:40.480
Beth: Can you think of any other famous
examples of people who are public about

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:44.130
being on the spectrum, perhaps they are
someone who may have been misunderstood

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:48.349
or misinterpreted in the past, or perhaps
they have always been understood and

00:03:48.349 --> 00:03:50.440
appreciated for what makes them, them.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:54.979
Try researching into other public
figures and their experiences with

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:59.600
Autism Spectrum Disorder and see what
you find, you never know, some examples

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:01.380
may reflect someone in a new light.

